Gives the simulated Mid360 the IMU the real one has inside it.

Generated against unitree_mujoco ae6a8403e272733e9996ef59990880330496177f.

FAST-LIO fuses the IMU that shares a housing with the laser, and until this patch the
simulator had none there, so the pelvis IMU stood in for it. That does not work on this
robot: waist_yaw, waist_roll and waist_pitch lie between pelvis and torso_link, the
walking policy owns all three (walk_policy.hpp: "legs 0-11 plus waist 12-14"), and they
move through 25, 9 and 16 degrees respectively while walking. FAST-LIO takes ONE constant
lidar-to-IMU extrinsic, so across that chain no value is right and the scan match came
apart whenever the robot turned.

The site sits where g1_description puts mid360_imu -- the mid360_joint mount composed with
Livox's published lidar-in-IMU offset [-0.011, -0.02329, 0.04412] -- and carries the same
orientation as mid360_link, because both sensors sit in one housing and flip together with
the upside-down mount. That makes the simulator's extrinsic Livox's own constant, the same
number the hardware config uses.

SENSORS APPENDED AT THE END of the block, which is load-bearing: unitree_sdk2_bridge reads
motor state as three contiguous nu-sized blocks of sensordata and everything after by
resolved address, so appending shifts nothing it indexes. Nothing new is actuated and nu is
untouched, so RobotBridge's fixed 35-motor arrays are unaffected -- same constraint the
Dex3 patch works under.

NO NOISE MODEL, deliberately. The pelvis IMU the model already carries has none either, so
adding it here would make the two sensors incomparable and would change what a drift
measurement means in the same commit that changes where the IMU is. Livox specify the
ICM40609's noise; adding it is a separate, measurable change.

diff --git a/unitree_robots/g1/g1_29dof.xml b/unitree_robots/g1/g1_29dof.xml
index 2aa7600..2ed4e3a 100644
--- a/unitree_robots/g1/g1_29dof.xml
+++ b/unitree_robots/g1/g1_29dof.xml
@@ -239,6 +239,11 @@
             mesh="waist_roll_link" />
           <site name="secondary_imu" size="0.01" pos="-0.03959 -0.00224 0.13792"/>
           <body name="torso_link" pos="0 0 0.019">
+            <!-- The IMU inside the Mid360. Pose mirrors g1_description's mid360_imu frame: the
+                 mid360_joint mount composed with Livox's lidar-in-IMU offset, and the sensor's
+                 own upside-down orientation, because both sit in one housing. -->
+            <site name="mid360_imu" size="0.01" pos="0.013523592 -0.02326 0.471934279"
+                  quat="0 0.99967335 0 -0.02555756"/>
             <inertial pos="0.00331658 0.000261533 0.179856"
               quat="0.999831 0.000376204 0.0179895 -0.00377704" mass="9.598"
               diaginertia="0.12407 0.111951 0.0325382" />
@@ -629,6 +634,10 @@
     <framequat name="secondary_imu_quat" objtype="site" objname="secondary_imu" />
     <gyro name="secondary_imu_gyro" site="secondary_imu" noise="5e-4" cutoff="34.9"/>
     <accelerometer name="secondary_imu_acc" site="secondary_imu" noise="1e-2" cutoff="157"/>
+
+    <framequat name="mid360_imu_quat" objtype="site" objname="mid360_imu" />
+    <gyro name="mid360_imu_gyro" site="mid360_imu" />
+    <accelerometer name="mid360_imu_acc" site="mid360_imu" />
   </sensor>
 
 </mujoco>
